        {
          "type": "context",
          "id": "YYqc7",
          "x": 16510,
          "y": 57,
          "name": "Context",
          "width": 250,
          "height": 219,
          "content": "Disconnected State UX Rationale\n\nWe use a single info-style toast: 'New data may be available' with a Refresh button.\n\nWhy this approach:\n- Non-alarming: user's data is still visible and usable, just potentially stale\n- User control: Refresh button lets the user decide when to act\n- Focuses on what matters to the user (data freshness) not system internals (connection lost)\n- Not a blocking error — cached/loaded data remains fully visible\n- Single toast handles the entire disconnected state cleanly without multiple warning/error escalation stages"
        }
      ]
    },
